WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.177 --> 00:00:13.017
idea was this.

2
00:00:13.658 --> 00:00:15.259
He thought of someone who needed help.

3
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.121
He thought of someone who was lonely and lost.

4
00:00:18.902 --> 00:00:20.583
He thought of someone who needed a friend.

5
00:00:21.304 --> 00:00:22.645
He thought of an orphanage.

6
00:00:24.547 --> 00:00:27.149
Pinocchio knew how it felt not to have a family.

7
00:00:27.909 --> 00:00:31.052
Many strangers had been kind to him and had given him a lot.

8
00:00:31.572 --> 00:00:37.274
And he remembered the Blue Fairy saying, "It is a great thing to receive help from a stranger,

9
00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:41.395
but it is an even greater thing to give help to a stranger."

10
00:00:41.415 --> 00:00:47.317
"I am going to help children who don't have a mom or dad," he decided.

11
00:00:48.457 --> 00:00:50.898
Pinocchio eventually found his way to an orphanage.

12
00:00:51.598 --> 00:00:54.659
It was small, and there were many dead trees in the yard.

13
00:00:54.679 --> 00:00:58.560
"I will help move these trees," Pinocchio said.

14
00:00:59.552 --> 00:01:01.614
He looped a rope around a tree and pulled.

15
00:01:02.374 --> 00:01:05.117
He did this for every tree until the yard was clean.

16
00:01:07.038 --> 00:01:09.780
The children saw him in the yard and ran outside.

17
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.063
"Yay, a donkey!"

18
00:01:13.403 --> 00:01:13.944
they cried.

19
00:01:13.964 --> 00:01:17.927
"What a nice donkey," one girl said.

20
00:01:17.947 --> 00:01:20.409
"Could we ride on your back, Mr.

21
00:01:20.449 --> 00:01:22.030
Donkey?" she asked.

22
00:01:22.691 --> 00:01:25.013
Pinocchio nodded, and the girl climbed on.

23
00:01:25.873 --> 00:01:28.916
One by one, he gave the children rides around the yard.

24
00:01:29.492 --> 00:01:31.273
They laughed and were very happy.

25
00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:36.735
When it was dinnertime, the children ran inside to eat macaroni.

26
00:01:37.595 --> 00:01:40.096
Pinocchio was hungry, and he wanted to be inside.

27
00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:42.317
But he also wanted to be generous.

28
00:01:43.037 --> 00:01:45.158
So he ate grass and slept outside.

29
00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.340
Every day, Pinocchio worked at the orphanage.

30
00:01:51.181 --> 00:01:53.782
He gave the children rides into town to buy food.

31
00:01:54.762 --> 00:01:57.463
He cropped the grass short so the children could play safely.

32
00:01:58.064 --> 00:01:59.064
He carried firewood.

33
00:01:59.772 --> 00:02:03.334
If there was any hard job to do, Pinocchio was happy to help.

34
00:02:06.316 --> 00:02:10.978
In the afternoons, he would sit outside the house and listen to the children study their lessons.

35
00:02:10.998 --> 00:02:14.580
"Children, what is two plus two?"

36
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.161
the teacher asked.

37
00:02:16.181 --> 00:02:19.062
"Four!" they all shouted.

38
00:02:19.082 --> 00:02:23.005
"Children, where is our nation's capital?"

39
00:02:23.445 --> 00:02:24.225
the teacher asked.

40
00:02:24.245 --> 00:02:26.747
"Rome!" they all shouted.

41
00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:29.108
"Good," the teacher said.

42
00:02:29.796 --> 00:02:31.597
"Now, it is time for a story."

43
00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:35.539
Pinocchio loved the teacher's stories, so he listened carefully.

44
00:02:35.559 --> 00:02:38.601
"Once there was a man named Jonah.

45
00:02:39.181 --> 00:02:42.443
He tried to disobey God, and he ran away.

46
00:02:43.323 --> 00:02:45.244
But he was swallowed by a whale!

47
00:02:46.145 --> 00:02:48.266
He lived in the whale for three days.

48
00:02:49.026 --> 00:02:53.889
He was sorry for disobeying God, so the whale spit him onto a beach.

49
00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:57.051
We must always obey God, children."

50
00:02:58.171 --> 00:02:59.172
Pinocchio sat up.

51
00:03:00.236 --> 00:03:01.938
"Jonah lived inside a whale?

52
00:03:02.558 --> 00:03:03.359
Of course!

53
00:03:03.999 --> 00:03:06.561
Father must be living inside the whale too!

54
00:03:07.702 --> 00:03:10.084
The Blue Fairy said he was safe and hidden.

55
00:03:10.725 --> 00:03:12.126
That must be where he is!

56
00:03:13.107 --> 00:03:15.208
Oh, if only I had stayed in school.

57
00:03:15.969 --> 00:03:18.391
I would have learned this story a long time ago.

58
00:03:18.971 --> 00:03:20.953
I could have saved Father faster!"

59
00:03:22.294 --> 00:03:25.477
Just as Pinocchio said this, a big change happened.

60
00:03:26.037 --> 00:03:27.518
His hooves changed to fingers.

61
00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:29.340
His ears got small again.

62
00:03:30.248 --> 00:03:31.209
His fur fell off.

63
00:03:31.869 --> 00:03:33.730
And he sounded like a boy again.

64
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.210
"It worked!"

65
00:03:35.611 --> 00:03:36.151
he cried.

66
00:03:36.171 --> 00:03:38.232
"The Blue Fairy was right!

67
00:03:38.872 --> 00:03:40.953
I was generous and worked hard.

68
00:03:41.533 --> 00:03:43.174
Now, I can be a boy again!"

69
00:03:44.455 --> 00:03:47.796
Pinocchio ran to the ocean as fast as his wooden legs would go.

70
00:03:48.737 --> 00:03:53.499
He was not going to stop this time, not for gold or a circus or Paradisle.

71
00:03:54.479 --> 00:03:55.720
He was going to find Geppetto!
